   "source": [
    "# Notebook 03: Statistical Analysis & Hypothesis Testing\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business & Methodological Context\n",
    "Before building predictive ML models, risk managers must validate whether observed relationships between risk factors and default rates are statistically significant or merely sampling noise. We employ rigorous statistical tests (Chi-Square, Two-Sample Independent t-Test, Pearson Correlation) with explicit null ($H_0$) and alternative ($H_1$) hypotheses."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from scipy import stats\n",
    "\n",
    "customers_df = pd.read_csv('../data/raw/customers.csv')\n",
    "credit_df = pd.read_csv('../data/raw/credit_history.csv')\n",
    "emp_df = pd.read_csv('../data/raw/employment_history.csv')\n",
    "apps_df = pd.read_csv('../data/raw/applications.csv')\n",
    "\n",
    "df = apps_df.merge(customers_df, on='customer_id') \\\n",
    "            .merge(credit_df, on='customer_id') \\\n",
    "            .merge(emp_df, on='customer_id')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded dataset with {len(df):,} total rows.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Hypothesis Test 1: Two-Sample t-Test (Credit Score vs Default Target)\n",
    "- **$H_0$**: The mean credit score of defaulting borrowers is equal to non-defaulting borrowers ($\mu_{\\text{default}} = \mu_{\\text{non-default}}$).\n",
    "- **$H_1$**: The mean credit score of defaulting borrowers is significantly lower than non-defaulting borrowers ($\mu_{\\text{default}} < \mu_{\\text{non-default}}$).\n",
    "- **Alpha**: $\\alpha = 0.05$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "scores_default = df[df['default_target'] == 1]['credit_score']\n",
    "scores_non_default = df[df['default_target'] == 0]['credit_score']\n",
    "\n",
    "t_stat, p_val = stats.ttest_ind(scores_default, scores_non_default, equal_var=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Mean Credit Score (Default=1): {scores_default.mean():.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mean Credit Score (Default=0): {scores_non_default.mean():.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"t-Statistic: {t_stat:.4f}, p-Value: {p_val:.4e}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if p_val < 0.05:\n",
    "    print(\"Conclusion: Reject H0. The mean credit score of defaulting borrowers is significantly lower.\")\n",
    "    print(\"Business Meaning: Credit score is a highly valid statistical predictor of default risk.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Conclusion: Fail to reject H0.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Hypothesis Test 2: Chi-Square Test of Independence (Recent Delinquency vs Default)\n",
    "- **$H_0$**: Recent delinquency status and loan default outcome are independent.\n",
    "- **$H_1$**: Recent delinquency status and loan default outcome are dependent.\n",
    "- **Alpha**: $\\alpha = 0.05$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "contingency_table = pd.crosstab(df['recent_delinquency'], df['default_target'])\n",
    "chi2_stat, p_val_chi, dof, expected = stats.chi2_contingency(contingency_table)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Contingency Table:\")\n",
    "print(contingency_table)\n",
    "print(f\"Chi2 Statistic: {chi2_stat:.4f}, Degrees of Freedom: {dof}, p-Value: {p_val_chi:.4e}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if p_val_chi < 0.05:\n",
    "    print(\"Conclusion: Reject H0. Recent delinquency is strongly associated with default outcome.\")\n",
    "    print(\"Business Meaning: Prior delinquency within the past 6 months must serve as a major underwriting trigger.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Conclusion: Fail to reject H0.\")"
   ]
  }
